1
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
The Trench is a war, history film directed by William Boyd.

2
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
The Trench tells the story of a group of young British soldiers on the eve of the Battle of
the Somme in the summer of 1916, the worst defeat in British military history.

3
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Against this ill-fated backdrop, the movie depicts the soldiers' experience as a mixture of
boredom, fear, panic, and restlessness, confined to a trench on the front lines.

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Sgt. Telford Winter, played by Daniel Craig.

5
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Lance Cpl. Victor Dell, played by Danny Dyer.

6
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Pte. Colin Daventry, played by James D'Arcy.

7
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Pte. Billy Macfarlane, played by Paul Nicholls.

8
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
2nd Lt. Ellis Harte, played by Julian Rhind-Tutt.

9
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Pte. Charlie Ambrose, played by Ciarán McMenamin.

10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The Trench is a 1999 war film written and directed by William
Boyd and starring Paul Nicholls and Daniel Craig.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
It depicts the experiences of a group of young British soldiers in the
48 hours leading up to the Battle of the Somme in 1916.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
James D'Arcy, Cillian Murphy and Ben Whishaw also appear.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The film explores themes of friendship, world war i,
bravery, trauma, based on true story.
